      "title": "Plans for Tomorrow",
      "focus": "ir a + infinitive",
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "objectives": [
        "talk about immediate future plans",
        "ask what someone is going to do",
        "combine a plan with a time and place"
      ],
      "teaching": {
        "explanation": "The high-frequency future pattern is ir a + infinitive: voy a estudiar, vas a trabajar, va a comer. It is more useful at this level than memorizing the full simple future.",
        "pattern": "Voy a estudiar mañana. ¿Qué vas a hacer? = What are you going to do?",
        "note": "The preposition a appears twice in many travel/planning phrases: voy a Madrid; voy a estudiar."
      },
